From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Spatiand build <claude@prasetya.id>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 01:51:33 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Spatiand: the PDF viewer in the room's own look, and no
 Google Drive button

The owner, 2026-11-27, choosing Chromium's own PDF tools for SpatiLoupe's PDFs (shown through
SpatiMesh in its window): "yes restyle" -- with "uniform design language" with the room's
applications. The viewer's toolbar, side panels, menus, fields and the ground around the pages take
the room's look (crates/spatiand-app's ui::theme: its ground, panel, ink, hint, mark, selection,
separator; Roboto), defined once in shared_vars.css and followed by the viewer's own variables; dark
as the room is by default and light as its look says (prefers-color-scheme, which SpatiMesh takes
from the room, patch 0014), where the viewer was dark only. The page and zoom fields are the room's
quiet rounded fields. The ground around the pages (pdf_viewer.ts, and the first frame's,
pdf_util.cc) is the room's. Save to Google Drive is off by default (kPdfSaveToDrive): nothing of
Google's in the room.
